  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 355 PM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nNorth to northwest flow prevails through the weekend and into \nMonday, with a weak shortwave expected to move through the area \nSaturday. Scattered precipitation will accompany this wave, with \nwintry mix or snow expected, mainly along and north of Highway 200. \nNorthwest winds increase during the late morning and afternoon, with \ngusts up to 30 mph. The combination of falling snow and gusty \nnorthwest winds could bring brief periodic visibility reductions. \nThis will depend on the intensity of potential heavier snow showers, \nwith the highest probability being in the northern Red River Valley \nand northwest Minnesota. \n\nA surge of cold air follows the shortwave, with highs in the 20s \nSunday afternoon and lows falling into the teens Sunday night. H5 \nflow turns nearly zonal by Tuesday, allowing temperatures to climb \ninto the 30s and low 40s through the remainder of next week.",
